title: Walk_Socrates_Chrysostom
tags: walk
speaker: Socrates
---
Socrates: You asked who cares whether a virtual world is real.
Socrates: That response turns our attention from abstract metaphysics to human value.
Socrates: We walk now toward the shaded grove of Value Theory.
Socrates: The path climbs gently past red mushrooms and swaying grass.
Socrates: We must ask what truly matters in a human life.
Socrates: John Chrysostom waits in the clearing just ahead.
Socrates: Known for his golden speech, he taught that virtue and soul-care define well-being.
Socrates: He will ask whether virtual pleasures can satisfy a soul built for truth and virtue.
Socrates: Consider what gives genuine worth to your choices and actions.
Socrates: Step forward into his grove to explore what makes life good.
===
